<title>USA: Boise Cascade Q4 shr loss $0.16 vs profit.</title>
<headline>Boise Cascade Q4 shr loss $0.16 vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>BOISE, Idaho 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>BOISE CASCADE CORPORATION INCOME SUMMARY</p>
<p>				    (unaudited)</p>
<p>			  Three months ended December 31</p>
<p>						   1996		 1995</p>
<p> Sales				$1,262,740,000   $1,241,960,000</p>
<p> Net income				2,140,000	 70,420,000</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per common share</p>
<p> Primary					 (.16)		 1.15</p>
<p> Fully diluted				 (.16)		 1.07</p>
<p>			    Year ended December 31</p>
<p>						    1996		1995</p>
<p> Sales				 5,108,220,000    5,074,230,000</p>
<p> Net income				9,050,000	351,860,000</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per common share</p>
<p> Primary					 (.63)		 5.93</p>
<p> Fully diluted				 (.63)		 5.39</p>
<p> Average primary shares	     48,277,000	 55,028,000</p>
<p> Average fully diluted shares     48,277,000	 61,351,000</p>
<p>NOTE: Q4 1996 includes several one-time transactions resulting in a net increase to net income of $10.7 million, or 22 cents per fully diluted share.</p>
<p>1995 also includes several one-time adjustments that increased net income by $15.1 million and fully diluted earnings per share 25 cents for the year.</p>
<p>The computation of fully diluted net loss for the three months and year ended December 31, 1996, was antidilutive; therefore, the amounts reported for primary and fully diluted loss are the same.</p>
</text>
